{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/how-a-fridge-keeps-food-fresh/audio/main-29f066bc58f2.mp3","durationSec":78.48,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":2.64,"text":"Some bacteria are tiny germs that can make people sick."},{"start":2.64,"end":5.62,"text":"Many bacteria grow quickly when food is warm."},{"start":5.62,"end":10.74,"text":"Food-safety guides call 4°C to 60°C the Danger Zone."},{"start":11.54,"end":14.2,"text":"A fridge should keep food at 4°C or colder."},{"start":14.98,"end":18.44,"text":"The cold does not kill all bacteria, but it slows their growth."},{"start":19.04,"end":20.58,"text":"This helps food stay safe longer."},{"start":21.2,"end":25.56,"text":"The FDA says a fridge should be at 4°C (40°F) or colder."},{"start":26.2,"end":30.38,"text":"A freezer should be at -18°C (0°F) or colder."},{"start":31.16,"end":33.3,"text":"A fridge dial may not show the real temperature."},{"start":33.96,"end":36.46,"text":"Put a fridge thermometer inside and check it often."},{"start":37.22,"end":41,"text":"Do not pack the fridge too tightly, because cold air needs room to move."},{"start":41.96,"end":44.62,"text":"Raw meat, poultry, seafood, and eggs can carry germs."},{"start":44.92,"end":47.74,"text":"The CDC says to keep these foods separate from other food."},{"start":48.14,"end":51.72,"text":"Put raw meat or seafood in a sealed container so its juice cannot leak."},{"start":52.48,"end":55.08,"text":"Keep other foods in covered containers or sealed bags."},{"start":55.66,"end":58.48,"text":"Clean spills in the fridge quickly so germs do not spread."},{"start":59.6,"end":62.82,"text":"The CDC says to refrigerate food that can spoil within two hours."},{"start":63.74,"end":68.94,"text":"If the food is in heat above 32°C (90°F), refrigerate it within one hour."},{"start":69.88,"end":73.54,"text":"Put a large amount of warm food into several clean, shallow containers."},{"start":74.72,"end":75.84,"text":"Small amounts cool faster."},{"start":76.62,"end":77.94,"text":"Then put them in the fridge promptly."}],"words":[{"text":"Some","start":0,"end":0.24},{"text":"bacteria","start":0.24,"end":0.6},{"text":"are","start":0.6,"end":0.92},{"text":"tiny","start":0.92,"end":1.24},{"text":"germs","start":1.24,"end":1.62},{"text":"that","start":1.62,"end":1.74},{"text":"can","start":1.74,"end":1.88},{"text":"make","start":1.88,"end":2.02},{"text":"people","start":2.02,"end":2.28},{"text":"sick","start":2.28,"end":2.64},{"text":"Many","start":2.64,"end":3.58},{"text":"bacteria","start":3.58,"end":4.04},{"text":"grow","start":4.04,"end":4.36},{"text":"quickly","start":4.36,"end":4.72},{"text":"when","start":4.72,"end":4.96},{"text":"food","start":4.96,"end":5.14},{"text":"is","start":5.14,"end":5.3},{"text":"warm","start":5.3,"end":5.62},{"text":"Food-safety","start":5.62,"end":6.76},{"text":"guides","start":6.76,"end":7.2},{"text":"call","start":7.2,"end":7.42},{"text":"4","start":7.42,"end":7.91},{"text":"C","start":7.91,"end":8.4},{"text":"to","start":8.4,"end":8.68},{"text":"60","start":8.68,"end":9.06},{"text":"C","start":9.06,"end":9.92},{"text":"the","start":9.92,"end":10.14},{"text":"Danger","start":10.14,"end":10.36},{"text":"Zone","start":10.36,"end":10.74},{"text":"A","start":11.54,"end":11.58},{"text":"fridge","start":11.58,"end":11.86},{"text":"should","start":11.86,"end":12.12},{"text":"keep","start":12.12,"end":12.3},{"text":"food","start":12.3,"end":12.54},{"text":"at","start":12.54,"end":12.68},{"text":"4","start":12.68,"end":13.16},{"text":"C","start":13.16,"end":13.64},{"text":"or","start":13.64,"end":13.9},{"text":"colder","start":13.9,"end":14.2},{"text":"The","start":14.98,"end":15.1},{"text":"cold","start":15.1,"end":15.4},{"text":"does","start":15.4,"end":15.6},{"text":"not","start":15.6,"end":15.88},{"text":"kill","start":15.88,"end":16.1},{"text":"all","start":16.1,"end":16.32},{"text":"bacteria","start":16.32,"end":16.74},{"text":"but","start":17.2,"end":17.46},{"text":"it","sta